Round-11 vendoring note (per .dejavue/timeline.jsonl):

The vendored crate ships BOTH `Widget for List` AND `StatefulWidget for List`
together with `ListState` as the canonical selection carrier. This is a
deliberate divergence from round-6 Tabs (which shipped Widget-only +
carved-out StatefulWidget due to E0034 ambiguity).

The module-level `//!` doc-comment in `src/lib.rs` documents the E0034
carve-out pattern:

  Pattern A - fully-qualified trait-method call:
    <List as StatefulWidget>::render(list, area, buf, &mut state);

  Pattern B - submodule namespace isolation:
    stateful::render(&list, area, buf, &mut state);

That disambiguates the call site when both trait impls are in scope.
The integration test `e0034_fully_qualified_resolve` proves Pattern A
compiles + paints at the fully-qualified call site - this is the
round-11 differentiator.

